Hi,

I'd like to turn this silly (deadly) situation into a learning
experience...

My Valkyrie was confidently going up to the last level of Sokoban.
Once there and after moving a few boulders, a friendly giant appeared!
Knowing that they can move boulders, and as there wasn't much room or
extra boulders, I decided to kill the poor guy. He didn't like this,
but instead of beating the hell out of me hand to hand, he decided to
show his contempt by playing bowling with a few spares he had! The
giant was easy to kill, but the two extra boulders in my way would
ruin the level completely...

At this point, and knowing that I died shortly afterwards, I should
give the bit of information that makes this a YASD and will probably
trigger some laughs: I did have a pick-axe in my bag.

Anyway, I didn't remember that then, so I decided to dump everything
to push boulders around. And so this naked girl squeezed between
boulders to try to save the situation, but she found a surprise there:
a lovely owlbear, who didn't hesitate to grab her and beat her to
death, despite the puny bare-handed hits of a pinky non-armored human.

My question is: apart from the obvious "stop for a few minutes and go
through your inventory before making decisions", what should I have
done if I hadn't have a pick-axe? I mean, maybe the giant killing was
avoidable? I'm not familiar to their behaviour, maybe I shouldn't have
worried about him moving boulders in the first place... opinions?

